## Project context

This project has two codelines, both pure TypeScript ES modules (strict mode, ES2022, `"type": "module"`) with vitest as the only test runner.

- **mocka** — source lives in `src/fares.ts`, tests in `test/fares.test.ts`. Exports: `fareFor`, `totalFor`, `BASE_FARE_CENTS`, `CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS`, type `Rider`.
- **mockb** — source lives in `src/schedule.ts`, tests in `test/schedule.test.ts`. Exports: `formatStops`, `totalMinutes`, type `Stop`.

Both codelines use the same npm scripts:
- `test` → `vitest run`
- `build` → `tsc --noEmit` (type-check only; no emit)
- `lint` → no-op (`echo no-lint-configured`) — there is no linter, so do not expect lint feedback.

The two tickets in scope are single-line boundary/off-by-one bugs in pure logic with no external dependencies:

- **MOCK3-1** (mocka): In `fareFor`, the senior concession check uses `rider.age > 65` instead of `>= 65`, so a rider aged exactly 65 is charged `BASE_FARE_CENTS` instead of `CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS`. The existing test suite covers age 70 but not the 65 boundary.
- **MOCK3-2** (mockb): In `formatStops`, the loop condition `i < stops.length - 1` skips the last stop. It should be `i < stops.length`. The existing tests assert the arrow separator and the first stop name but do not assert the presence of the final stop.

